1
00:01:31,780 --> 00:01:35,070
[In my prime]

2
00:01:35,240 --> 00:01:37,630
[Episode 24]

3
00:01:38,120 --> 00:01:39,150
Childhood sweethearts

4
00:01:39,150 --> 00:01:40,200
have the most reliable bond

5
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:41,350
in the world.

6
00:01:44,509 --> 00:01:46,110
I mean, I know my sister well.

7
00:01:46,430 --> 00:01:47,710
Zhi definitely holds

8
00:01:47,710 --> 00:01:48,509
a special place

9
00:01:48,509 --> 00:01:49,240
in her heart.

10
00:01:50,350 --> 00:01:52,070
Zhi is single and Si is divorced.

11
00:01:52,070 --> 00:01:54,270
Why can't they rekindle their romance?

12
00:02:15,120 --> 00:02:17,470
[Prime Era]

13
00:02:17,550 --> 00:02:18,460
Mom!

14
00:02:19,400 --> 00:02:20,329
Doudou, Doudou.

15
00:02:21,840 --> 00:02:22,640
There, there.

16
00:02:25,079 --> 00:02:26,120
Stop crying.

17
00:02:27,240 --> 00:02:28,040
There, there.

18
00:02:30,190 --> 00:02:31,590
Doudou got bullied.

19
00:02:32,680 --> 00:02:33,750
When he played outside,

20
00:02:33,750 --> 00:02:34,840
some kids who didn't know better

21
00:02:34,840 --> 00:02:35,900
said he has no dad.

22
00:02:36,310 --> 00:02:37,710
How can you put up with it?

23
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:39,460
It's infuriating.

24
00:02:43,030 --> 00:02:43,520
Doudou.

25
00:02:45,030 --> 00:02:46,430
There, there, don't cry.

26
00:02:47,630 --> 00:02:48,760
Does your face hurt?

27
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:51,680
There, there.

28
00:02:51,680 --> 00:02:52,870
Wipe your tears.

29
00:02:54,310 --> 00:02:55,240
Wipe your tears.

30
00:02:56,560 --> 00:02:57,890
Ignore their nonsense.

31
00:02:58,150 --> 00:02:59,750
Who says you don't have a dad?

32
00:02:59,840 --> 00:03:00,560
It's just that your dad

33
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:02,090
doesn't live with your mom.

34
00:03:03,150 --> 00:03:04,280
Mom...

35
00:03:05,120 --> 00:03:06,490
Alright, alright.

36
00:03:06,630 --> 00:03:07,430
There, there.

37
00:03:07,910 --> 00:03:08,650
Besides,

38
00:03:08,680 --> 00:03:10,340
you not only have your father,

39
00:03:10,590 --> 00:03:11,680
but your uncle, and me.

40
00:03:11,680 --> 00:03:12,190
Right?

41
00:03:13,910 --> 00:03:14,630
How about this?

42
00:03:14,630 --> 00:03:15,640
Tell me which little brats said it.

43
00:03:15,640 --> 00:03:16,500
Take me to them.

44
00:03:16,590 --> 00:03:18,190
I'll talk some sense into them.

45
00:03:18,190 --> 00:03:18,890
It's okay.

46
00:03:19,710 --> 00:03:21,510
Their parents have apologized.

47
00:03:21,800 --> 00:03:23,360
Doudou just hasn't

48
00:03:24,470 --> 00:03:25,590
gotten over it yet.

49
00:03:27,120 --> 00:03:28,190
Mom...

50
00:03:28,430 --> 00:03:28,910
Doudou,

51
00:03:29,520 --> 00:03:30,380
how about this?

52
00:03:30,560 --> 00:03:32,110
I'll teach you boxing, okay?

53
00:03:32,110 --> 00:03:33,120
Once you master it,

54
00:03:33,120 --> 00:03:34,390
you can protect yourself

55
00:03:34,390 --> 00:03:36,120
if they dare to bully you again.

56
00:03:36,240 --> 00:03:36,660
Okay?

57
00:03:36,960 --> 00:03:37,360
Okay.

58
00:03:37,750 --> 00:03:38,210
Come on.

59
00:03:40,120 --> 00:03:40,650
Good boy.

60
00:03:42,030 --> 00:03:42,760
Come with me.

61
00:03:44,470 --> 00:03:44,920
Here.

62
00:03:45,079 --> 00:03:45,880
Come, Doudou.

63
00:03:45,910 --> 00:03:47,770
Move a bit over. Stand right here.

64
00:03:47,840 --> 00:03:49,500
Good. Stand still right here.

65
00:03:50,030 --> 00:03:51,150
Let's try three moves, alright?

66
00:03:51,150 --> 00:03:52,000
Repeat after me.

67
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:52,930
Stand straight.

68
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:54,079
Put your hands in position.

69
00:03:54,079 --> 00:03:55,210
Alright. Get ready.

70
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:56,360
Military boxing.

71
00:03:56,710 --> 00:03:57,710
Ready for combat!

72
00:03:59,710 --> 00:04:00,630
Yes. Stretch that leg out

73
00:04:00,630 --> 00:04:01,430
a little more.

74
00:04:01,840 --> 00:04:02,840
Good. Let's do it.

75
00:04:02,840 --> 00:04:04,710
The first move, lunge and punch!

76
00:04:06,150 --> 00:04:07,750
Throat strike and snap kick!

77
00:04:08,870 --> 00:04:10,200
Close-range uppercut!

78
00:04:11,150 --> 00:04:12,190
Side thrust kick!

79
00:04:13,910 --> 00:04:15,170
Turn and swing the arm!

80
00:04:16,360 --> 00:04:18,019
Empty stance chop to the ribs!

81
00:04:18,720 --> 00:04:19,240
Alright?

82
00:04:19,240 --> 00:04:20,390
Retract your leg after the kick.

83
00:04:20,390 --> 00:04:20,850
Come on,

84
00:04:20,920 --> 00:04:21,450
kick now.

85
00:04:22,160 --> 00:04:23,290
Good. That's right.

86
00:04:23,390 --> 00:04:24,360
You're doing it right.

87
00:04:24,360 --> 00:04:25,510
Good. Do it again.

88
00:04:26,190 --> 00:04:26,800
Very good.

89
00:04:29,430 --> 00:04:30,830
Here comes the next move.

90
00:04:30,920 --> 00:04:32,409
We'll start from this position.

91
00:04:32,409 --> 00:04:33,040
One more time.

92
00:04:33,040 --> 00:04:34,440
Get set. One, two, three.

93
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:36,130
Good. That's right.

94
00:04:36,360 --> 00:04:36,890
Alright.

95
00:04:37,390 --> 00:04:39,070
Let's continue from this posture.

96
00:04:39,070 --> 00:04:42,070
The third move, horizontal strike
from horse stance!

97
00:04:44,270 --> 00:04:45,310
Mind this arm.

98
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:47,460
Right. Swing it like this.

99
00:04:48,070 --> 00:04:48,430
Okay?

100
00:04:49,560 --> 00:04:49,890
Come on.

101
00:04:49,890 --> 00:04:50,600
Let's repeat

102
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:51,659
these three moves.

103
00:04:52,560 --> 00:04:53,920
Come on. Get ready.

104
00:04:54,510 --> 00:04:56,040
L-Let's start from here.

105
00:05:09,310 --> 00:05:09,750
Hello?

106
00:05:10,360 --> 00:05:12,360
Zhi, let's go to the movies tonight.

107
00:05:12,480 --> 00:05:13,410
Go to the movies?

108
00:05:13,740 --> 00:05:14,560
What movie?

109
00:05:15,830 --> 00:05:16,360
Hello?

110
00:05:16,430 --> 00:05:18,240
Si, let's go to the movies tonight.

111
00:05:18,240 --> 00:05:18,840
What time?

112
00:05:19,040 --> 00:05:19,510
At 8:00.

113
00:05:20,560 --> 00:05:22,620
Don't worry about it. See you at 8:00.

114
00:05:23,560 --> 00:05:23,920
Fine.

115
00:05:26,260 --> 00:05:27,990
Okay. I'll bring Doudou along.

116
00:05:28,360 --> 00:05:29,420
It's settled then.

117
00:05:29,630 --> 00:05:30,160
Alright.

118
00:05:37,800 --> 00:05:38,750
What's with him?

119
00:05:39,040 --> 00:05:40,040
Is he seasick?

120
00:05:41,270 --> 00:05:42,390
Seasick, huh?

121
00:05:43,360 --> 00:05:44,040
Isn't he?

122
00:05:44,060 --> 00:05:45,320
You want some popcorn?

123
00:05:45,990 --> 00:05:47,640
Eat it. Just a piece.

124
00:05:52,250 --> 00:05:53,630
Is he seasick?

125
00:05:55,720 --> 00:05:56,950
I-If you find it inappropriate,

126
00:05:56,950 --> 00:05:58,280
m-maybe I should leave.

127
00:06:01,270 --> 00:06:02,530
The movie has started.

128
00:06:02,950 --> 00:06:04,350
Let's watch it together.

129
00:06:15,160 --> 00:06:16,600
It's fun, isn't it?

130
00:06:18,430 --> 00:06:18,920
Careful.

131
00:06:18,920 --> 00:06:20,320
Don't spill the popcorn.

132
00:06:23,840 --> 00:06:25,040
Let me hold it for you.

133
00:06:25,350 --> 00:06:28,580
♪ In spring, the bright red flowers ♪

134
00:06:28,610 --> 00:06:31,930
♪ Bloom high, filling every branch ♪

135
00:06:31,950 --> 00:06:37,340
♪ Quietly waiting for
someone to pick them by hand ♪

136
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:39,120
One more piece, Doudou?

137
00:06:38,550 --> 00:06:41,830
♪ In summer, the little one ♪

138
00:06:41,860 --> 00:06:45,330
♪ Quietly leaves home ♪

139
00:06:45,360 --> 00:06:50,830
♪ Gently hanging the key upon the door ♪

140
00:06:48,080 --> 00:06:48,950
Feed me one.

141
00:06:52,240 --> 00:06:55,840
♪ In autumn, beneath the shining stars ♪

142
00:06:55,860 --> 00:06:59,090
♪ The year’s harvest is full ♪

143
00:06:56,360 --> 00:06:58,290
I heard this movie is pretty funny.

144
00:06:59,110 --> 00:07:05,580
♪ Across countless mountains and rivers,
I keep thinking of my parents ♪

145
00:07:04,160 --> 00:07:05,890
Perfect for us to enjoy together.

146
00:07:05,890 --> 00:07:08,990
♪ In winter, through the biting winds ♪

147
00:07:09,210 --> 00:07:12,520
♪ Amid the cold and ice ♪

148
00:07:12,560 --> 00:07:18,210
♪ Those who have gone far
from home disappear without a trace ♪

149
00:07:20,220 --> 00:07:23,720
♪ The key is at the door ♪

150
00:07:23,740 --> 00:07:26,210
♪ Whoever sees it will understand ♪

151
00:07:26,780 --> 00:07:30,210
♪ My dear, please take good care ♪

152
00:07:30,240 --> 00:07:33,220
♪ Don’t let the waiting be in vain ♪

153
00:07:33,650 --> 00:07:37,040
♪ Goodbye was left unspoken ♪

154
00:07:37,070 --> 00:07:40,050
♪ All that remains is a longing face ♪

155
00:07:40,350 --> 00:07:46,970
♪ When spring returns,
please raise a glass for me ♪

